How the pieces are intended to connect. This is a proposed design. It does not describe a deployed service, contract, or integration. EraX Social shows the post and whether it is paid. EraX Creator holds the price, the access rule, and the creator's payment preferences. The wallet collects approval. A future contract, if written and reviewed, would record the payment on Base. An off-chain entitlement record would tell the application whether to show the content. // No contract is deployed.
// A future subscription call would be explicit, for example:
// subscribe(creator, planId) payable
// The user would see the network, value, and destination before signing.

What contracts would be responsible for, if they are written. This is a proposed design. It does not describe a deployed service, contract, or integration. The ERAX token contract is written as a fixed-supply ERC-20. It is not deployed and has no published address. A later contract set might record a payment, a subscription, or an ownership event. It should not store private messages or entire media files. Contracts in this design would be small, specific, and reviewed before any deployment. // There is no contract address.
// The ERAX token is specified and not deployed.
// There is no testnet deployment published on this site.

Guidance before any code is treated as production. This is a proposed design. It does not describe a deployed service, contract, or integration. If contracts are written, they should be versioned, tested, and reviewed. Documentation examples are not source releases. Do not point a frontend at an address copied from a document unless that address is published with matching source. // Not compiled. Not deployed.
interface CreatorPayment {
  function tip(address creator) external payable;
}
